	'about_0_h' => 'The founding story',
	'about_0_n' => '2014',
	'about_0_p1' => 'Ilse Varga opened the practice in Northvale in 2014 after twelve years in hospital rehab. The shoulders she kept seeing in clinic were not a mystery of the treatment room. They came from a desk: a chair set for the person who had sat there before, a screen below the eyes, a day with almost no change of position. That is still the reason the work exists. We watch a working desk before we recommend a change, and the thing we sell is the readiness review, booked before an office move, a furniture purchase, or a return to the office. On-site visits run within 40 km of Northvale. Remote desk reviews run anywhere. The studio is Unit 4, 18 Foundry Row, Northvale.',
	'about_1_h' => 'Watch first',
	'about_1_n' => '01 / 03',
	'about_1_p1' => 'The first principle is to watch before recommending. A readiness review begins with the person already at the desk, not with a catalogue and not with a plan of furniture that has not been sat in. We look at how the chair, the screen and the floor are actually used on that day. Light, noise, routes and the shape of the working day are part of the same look. Nothing is written as a change until someone has seen the desk in use. The visit is there so the recommendation can be small, specific and tied to a person, rather than a general picture of an office.',
	'about_2_h' => 'Change the least',
	'about_2_n' => '02 / 03',
	'about_2_p1' => 'The second principle is to change the least. We adjust what is already there before anyone is asked to buy. Seat height, armrests, a monitor arm, the position of a keyboard, where a person sits relative to a window: those are the usual first moves. A purchase list appears in the written plan only when the desk cannot be made fit with what the team already owns. We do not sell furniture and we do not take commission on what a client later buys. If a medical condition needs a diagnosis, we refer to a physiotherapist or a doctor. The review itself is not that diagnosis.',
	'about_3_h' => 'Write it down',
	'about_3_n' => '03 / 03',
	'about_3_p1' => 'The third principle is to write it down. Every change goes into a plan the team can keep after we leave: one page per desk, plus a floor summary. The person at the desk and the manager who asked for the review can both see what was adjusted and what, if anything, is worth buying. The plan is delivered within five working days of the visit. Six weeks later we come back for a check, ninety minutes on site, to see whether the written changes are still the ones in use. A note that lives only in a conversation does not survive a busy floor.',
	'about_4_h' => 'A day on a review',
	'about_4_p1' => 'Visit days are Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday, from 08:30 to 17:00 at your site. We arrive at 08:30 and walk the floor. Each person then gives us twenty minutes at their own desk while the rest of the team keeps working. A consultant covers up to fifteen desks in a day. At 16:30 we sit with the manager for the findings conversation. Friday is for reports only. The report is written over the next two days, and the plan is with you within five working days. Office hours at Unit 4 are Monday to Friday, 08:30 to 17:30. The phone line is open from 09:00 to 16:00 on those days.',
