	'inc_st' => 'Three parts of the same visit, written into one plan.',
	'intro_h' => 'We watch before we recommend',
	'intro_p1' => 'A readiness review is what we do before an office move, a furniture purchase or a return to the office. We sit with the people who will use the desks, and we look before we recommend. The point is to see the work as it is: chair, screen, light, noise and the way the day actually moves.',
	'intro_p2' => 'We do not sell furniture, take commission or diagnose medical conditions. If a person needs a physiotherapist or a doctor, we refer. You receive a written plan the team can keep, and a purchase list only when something is missing.',
	'journal_0_p1' => 'Desk notes cover the looking itself: what we watch in the first ten minutes, how a sit-stand desk is actually used, what a laptop on a kitchen table asks of a person. News covers the practice: the Next openings list, and the few changes in how a visit is booked. Posts are filed as ruled rows, newest first, with the date and the category beside the title. Categories in use are Desk notes and News. Tags follow the subject of the post, such as chairs, screens, sit-stand, breaks and openings. Nothing here is a substitute for a readiness review. A post can tell you what we look at. It cannot see your floor.',
